A||||5||RossT||loud fuel pump humming?||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||11-06-2001||01:12 AM||||The formula I just bought  had sat for several years.  The previous owner had the tank dropped and new pump put in, in order to get it running.  <P>The fuel pump is extremely loud. It does not matter if the tank is full or empty its just always humming very loud!!  It does quiet a little upon acceleration, but is the loudest<BR>at idle.  I replaced the fuel filter just to make sure it was ok, and its still loud.<P>Does a new fuel pump need to break in?  Or maybee a cheap aftermarket one was put in?<BR>Would you drop the tank and replace the pump?<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||11-06-2001||01:25 AM||||The pump is isolated through rubber bushings and supports. If they didn't install it correctly, it will make tons-o-noise.<P>TK||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||11-06-2001||02:49 AM||||Also, some el cheapo fuel pumps will make a god awful racket, so I personally would install a new GM pump.<P>Like Terry said, it may not have been properly installed, so dropping the tank might be a good idea anyways.  The daily driver '88 GT I have had a new fuel pump installed about a year before I bought it, but was noisy and failed on me.  It was a generic replacement and whoever installed it removed the pulsator thingy, so it was probably doomed from the start.  Again, I would drop the tank to check things out and replace the pump at the same time. <P>I have an extra GM fuel pump lying around......LMK if you might be interested.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||stsmithgt||11-06-2001||09:53 AM||||Sounds like the cheapo model.  Found out I had an after market one in mine, since it failed.  It has a GM one now.  It should be fairly quiet and shouldn't make noise after a few seconds of building up pressure before starting the car and at least other noises should be enough to cover over any noise the fuel pump would make while it maintains the pressure after the car is running.  OR I'm completely wrong and it's something else. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||11-09-2001||10:05 AM||||Thanks for the info guys.  I just realized<BR>that when I stop fast, the fuel pump buzzing sound stops until the gas has settled.  Also when I accelerate fast the noise stops until<BR>you reach a constant speed.  So I am thinking that the pump was installed wrong.  Maybee not even attached to the sending unit.<P>I did notice that the old filter I took off was a new acdelco one, so Iam also thinking that the previous owner had a gm delear drop the tank and replace the pump.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||RossT||11-12-2001||10:54 PM||||Poblem has been fixed!!  Found an aftermarket<BR>cater fuel pump in the tank!  Replaced it with a GM unit and all is well.<P>BTW This is the second time I have done a fuel pump on a fiero and it took 1/3 the time!<P>||||reg||1
